# YouTube cookies for .play / .video (bot-check bypass)
#
# WHY YOU NEED THIS:
# YouTube now blocks many download requests from cloud/datacenter servers
# (like Replit) with "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot" — even though
# the bot code itself is working correctly. This affects a large chunk of
# videos (tested and confirmed: some IDs work, most don't, without cookies).
# There is no reliable token-generator workaround for this in a server
# sandbox — real browser cookies are the fix YouTube itself points to.
#
# HOW TO GET REAL COOKIES (2 minutes):
# 1. Install a browser extension: "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY" (Chrome/Firefox).
# 2. Log into https://youtube.com in that browser with any Google account.
# 3. Open youtube.com, click the extension icon, click "Export" / "Copy".
# 4. Paste the exported content into a new file named exactly: cookies.txt
#    (same folder as this example file, i.e. AA-MD-Bot/cookies.txt)
# 5. Restart the bot workflow. .play and .video will auto-detect and use it.
#
# NOTES:
# - cookies.txt is already in .gitignore — it will never be committed.
# - Cookies expire after a while (weeks/months). If downloads start failing
#   again with "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot", just re-export fresh
#   cookies from your browser and replace the file.
# - Use a throwaway/secondary Google account, not your primary one.
